        "Let's look at the laws that followed. The Civil Rights Act of 1964 outlawed segregation in public places and discrimination in hiring. The Voting Rights Act of 1965 put federal power behind the 15th Amendment at last. Dr. King was assassinated in 1968.\n[[1964 and 1965: the two great acts.]]",
        "The movement won by nonviolence, by courts, by marches that made the country look at itself, and by ordinary people who kept going after being beaten and jailed. It was, in the plainest sense, the country being held to its own words.",
